<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanish Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hanish Islands are a group of volcanic islands in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>. Eritrea seized the largest, Greater Hanish, in December 1995, and the dispute was taken to international arbitration. In awards of 1998 and 1999 the tribunal gave most of the islands to Yemen and fixed the maritime boundary, while guaranteeing traditional fishing rights for Eritreans.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hanish-islands.jpg" alt="Hanish Islands" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS006-E-45506_-_View_of_Yemen_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
